            <div xml:id="d545">

                <pb facs="0412" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg408"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/3416: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-19T11:00:00+08:00">July 19, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 19—7:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>361. Shanghai’s 1003, July 18, 6 p.m. regarding protection American nationals at
                    Kiukiang, Kuling and Nanchang. I have nothing to add to what I have already said
                    in my 347, July 11, 4 p.m., unless the Department has specific instructions for
                    me.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai. Shanghai please relay to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
